{#
calendar/_proposal_response.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The answer to a proposed date: the card goes, and a toast says what happened.

Removed rather than replaced, which is where this differs from the invitation
stream. An RSVP leaves something behind to look at — the meeting still exists
and now carries an answer — whereas both answers here end the offer: yes made
an event, no made a refusal, and in each case there is nothing left to decide.
A card that stayed on screen showing a decision already taken would invite the
same person to take it again.

So the toast is the whole report, and it is the only place "an event now
exists" is said at all.

Variables:
  messageId     int
  toastMessage  string  translation key
  toastType     string  success | error
#}
<turbo-stream action="remove" target="proposal_card_{{ messageId }}"></turbo-stream>

<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            message: toastMessage|trans,
            type: toastType,
        } %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
